msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/examples-and-applications/extracted-outputs/57c071aa-e8ab-4b39-b5db-773016da2550-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We will start debugging on local simulators.\n"
msgstr "Kita akan mulai debugging di simulator lokal.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: msgid repeated on page, first translation kept
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We now set an initial set of parameters:\n"
msgstr "Sekarang kita tentukan set parameter awal:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can minimize this cost function to calculate optimal parameters\n"
msgstr "Kita bisa meminimalkan fungsi biaya ini untuk menghitung parameter optimal\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because this toy problem uses only two qubits, we can check this by using NumPy's linear algebra eigensolver.\n"
msgstr "Karena masalah contoh ini hanya menggunakan dua qubit, kita bisa memverifikasi ini dengan menggunakan solver nilai eigen aljabar linear dari NumPy.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As you can see, the result is extremely close to the ideal.\n"
msgstr "Seperti yang bisa Anda lihat, hasilnya sangat dekat dengan nilai ideal.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Experimenting to improve speed and accuracy {#experimenting-to-improve-speed-and-accuracy}"
msgstr "Bereksperimen untuk meningkatkan kecepatan dan akurasi {#experimenting-to-improve-speed-and-accuracy}"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Add reference state {#add-reference-state}"
msgstr "Tambah reference state {#add-reference-state}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the previous example we have not used any reference operator $U_R$. Now let us think about how the ideal eigenstate $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|00\\rangle + |11\\rangle)$ can be obtained. Consider the following circuit.\n"
msgstr "Pada contoh sebelumnya kita tidak menggunakan operator referensi $U_R$ apapun. Sekarang mari kita pikirkan bagaimana eigenstate ideal $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|00\\rangle + |11\\rangle)$ bisa diperoleh. Perhatikan Circuit berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/examples-and-applications/extracted-outputs/55b26ae7-ad26-4b54-b4f3-2004bb2db0c9-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/examples-and-applications/extracted-outputs/55b26ae7-ad26-4b54-b4f3-2004bb2db0c9-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can quickly check that this circuit gives us the desired state.\n"
msgstr "Kita bisa dengan cepat memeriksa bahwa Circuit ini memberi kita state yang diinginkan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now that we have seen how a circuit preparing the solution state looks like, it seems reasonable to use a Hadamard gate as a reference circuit, so that the full ansatz becomes:\n"
msgstr "Sekarang setelah kita melihat seperti apa Circuit yang mempersiapkan state solusi, tampaknya masuk akal untuk menggunakan Gate Hadamard sebagai Circuit referensi, sehingga ansatz lengkapnya menjadi:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/examples-and-applications/extracted-outputs/14e04c7a-e81f-41e1-b0cf-790954581be9-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/examples-and-applications/extracted-outputs/14e04c7a-e81f-41e1-b0cf-790954581be9-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For this new circuit, the ideal solution could be reached with all the parameters set to $0$, so this confirms that the choice of reference circuit is reasonable.\n"
msgstr "Untuk Circuit baru ini, solusi ideal bisa dicapai dengan semua parameter diset ke $0$, sehingga ini mengkonfirmasi bahwa pilihan Circuit referensi sudah masuk akal.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now let us compare the number of cost function evaluations, optimizer iterations and time taken with those of the previous attempt.\n"
msgstr "Sekarang mari kita bandingkan jumlah evaluasi fungsi biaya, iterasi optimizer, dan waktu yang dibutuhkan dengan percobaan sebelumnya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Using our optimal parameters to calculate the minimum eigenvalue:\n"
msgstr "Menggunakan parameter optimal kita untuk menghitung nilai eigen minimum:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Depending on your specific system, this may or may not result in an improvement in speed or accuracy in this very small scale example. The point is that starting with physically-motivated reference states becomes increasingly important in improving speed and accuracy as problems scale.\n"
msgstr "Tergantung sistem spesifik kamu, ini mungkin atau mungkin tidak menghasilkan peningkatan kecepatan atau akurasi dalam contoh skala kecil ini. Intinya adalah bahwa memulai dengan reference state yang termotivasi secara fisik menjadi semakin penting dalam meningkatkan kecepatan dan akurasi seiring skala masalah bertambah.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Change the initial point {#change-the-initial-point}"
msgstr "Ubah titik awal {#change-the-initial-point}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now that we have seen the effect of adding the reference state, we will go into what happens when we choose different initial points $\\vec{\\theta_0}$. In particular we will use $\\vec{\\theta_0}=(0,0,0,0,6,0,0,0)$ and $\\vec{\\theta_0}=(6,6,6,6,6,6,6,6,6)$.\n"
msgstr "Setelah melihat efek dari penambahan reference state, kita akan melihat apa yang terjadi ketika kita memilih titik awal $\\vec{\\theta_0}$ yang berbeda. Secara khusus kita akan menggunakan $\\vec{\\theta_0}=(0,0,0,0,6,0,0,0)$ dan $\\vec{\\theta_0}=(6,6,6,6,6,6,6,6,6)$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Remember that, as discussed when the reference state was introduced, the ideal solution would be found when all the parameters are $0$, so the first initial point should give fewer evaluations.\n"
msgstr "Ingat bahwa, seperti yang dibahas ketika reference state diperkenalkan, solusi ideal akan ditemukan ketika semua parameter adalah $0$, sehingga titik awal pertama seharusnya memberikan lebih sedikit evaluasi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Adjusting initial point to $\\vec{\\theta_0}=(6,6,6,6,6,6,6,6,6)$:\n"
msgstr "Menyesuaikan titik awal ke $\\vec{\\theta_0}=(6,6,6,6,6,6,6,6,6)$:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "By experimenting with different initial points, you might be able to achieve convergence faster and with fewer function evaluations.\n"
msgstr "Dengan bereksperimen menggunakan titik awal yang berbeda, kamu mungkin bisa mencapai konvergensi lebih cepat dan dengan lebih sedikit evaluasi fungsi.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Experimenting with different optimizers {#experimenting-with-different-optimizers}"
msgstr "Bereksperimen dengan optimizer yang berbeda {#experimenting-with-different-optimizers}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can adjust the optimizer using SciPy `minimize`'s `method` argument, with more options [found here](https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.optimize.minimize.html). We originally used a constrained minimizer (`COBYLA`). In this example, we'll explore using an unconstrained minimizer (`BFGS`) instead\n"
msgstr "Kita bisa menyesuaikan optimizer menggunakan argumen `method` dari `minimize` SciPy, dengan lebih banyak opsi [yang bisa ditemukan di sini](https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.optimize.minimize.html). Awalnya kita menggunakan minimizer dengan batasan (`COBYLA`). Dalam contoh ini, kita akan menjelajahi penggunaan minimizer tanpa batasan (`BFGS`) sebagai gantinya\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "VQD example {#vqd-example}"
msgstr "Contoh VQD {#vqd-example}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here we implement the Qiskit patterns framework, explicitly.\n"
msgstr "Di sini kita mengimplementasikan framework Qiskit patterns secara eksplisit.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"
msgstr "Langkah 1: Petakan input klasik ke masalah kuantum {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now instead of looking for only the lowest eigenvalue of our observables, we will look for all $4$, (where $k=4$).\n"
msgstr "Sekarang alih-alih hanya mencari nilai eigen terendah dari observable kita, kita akan mencari semua $4$, (di mana $k=4$).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Remember that the cost functions of VQD are:\n"
msgstr "Ingat bahwa fungsi biaya VQD adalah:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"C_{l}(\\vec{\\theta}) :=\n"
"\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle +\n"
"\\sum_{j=0}^{l-1}\\beta_j |\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})| \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^j})\\rangle  |^2\n"
"\\quad \\forall l\\in\\{1,\\cdots,k\\}=\\{1,\\cdots,4\\}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"C_{l}(\\vec{\\theta}) :=\n"
"\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle +\n"
"\\sum_{j=0}^{l-1}\\beta_j |\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})| \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^j})\\rangle  |^2\n"
"\\quad \\forall l\\in\\{1,\\cdots,k\\}=\\{1,\\cdots,4\\}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is particularly important because a vector $\\vec{\\beta}=(\\beta_0,\\cdots,\\beta_{k-1})$ (in this case $(\\beta_0, \\beta_1, \\beta_2, \\beta_3)$) must be passed as an argument when we define the `VQD` object.\n"
msgstr "Ini sangat penting karena vektor $\\vec{\\beta}=(\\beta_0,\\cdots,\\beta_{k-1})$ (dalam kasus ini $(\\beta_0, \\beta_1, \\beta_2, \\beta_3)$) harus dilewatkan sebagai argumen saat kita mendefinisikan objek `VQD`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Also, in Qiskit's implementation of VQD, instead of considering the effective observables described in the previous notebook, the fidelities $|\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})| \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^j})\\rangle  |^2$ are calculated directly via the `ComputeUncompute` algorithm, that leverages a `Sampler` primitive to sample the probability of obtaining $|0\\rangle$ for the circuit\n"
"$U_A^\\dagger(\\vec{\\theta})U_A(\\vec{\\theta^j})$. This works precisely because this probability is\n"
msgstr ""
"Juga, dalam implementasi VQD Qiskit, alih-alih mempertimbangkan observable efektif yang dijelaskan di notebook sebelumnya, fidelitas $|\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})| \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^j})\\rangle  |^2$ dihitung langsung melalui algoritma `ComputeUncompute`, yang memanfaatkan primitif `Sampler` untuk mengambil sampel probabilitas mendapatkan $|0\\rangle$ untuk Circuit\n"
"$U_A^\\dagger(\\vec{\\theta})U_A(\\vec{\\theta^j})$. Ini berhasil karena probabilitas ini adalah\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "p_0\n"
msgstr "p_0\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "& = |\\langle 0|U_A^\\dagger(\\vec{\\theta})U_A(\\vec{\\theta^j})|0\\rangle|^2 \\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr "& = |\\langle 0|U_A^\\dagger(\\vec{\\theta})U_A(\\vec{\\theta^j})|0\\rangle|^2 \\\\[1mm]\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "& = |\\big(\\langle 0|U_A^\\dagger(\\vec{\\theta})\\big)\\big(U_A(\\vec{\\theta^j})|0\\rangle\\big)|^2 \\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr "& = |\\big(\\langle 0|U_A^\\dagger(\\vec{\\theta})\\big)\\big(U_A(\\vec{\\theta^j})|0\\rangle\\big)|^2 \\\\[1mm]\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "& = |\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) |\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^j}) \\rangle|^2 \\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr "& = |\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) |\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^j}) \\rangle|^2 \\\\[1mm]\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/examples-and-applications/extracted-outputs/e4d59381-43ff-4322-a6f2-df55cef18536-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/examples-and-applications/extracted-outputs/e4d59381-43ff-4322-a6f2-df55cef18536-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let's start by examining the following observable:\n"
msgstr "Mari kita mulai dengan memeriksa observable berikut:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{O}_2 := 2 II - 3 XX + 2 YY - 4 ZZ\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{O}_2 := 2 II - 3 XX + 2 YY - 4 ZZ\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\left\\{\n"
"\\begin{array}{c}\n"
"\\lambda_0 = -7 \\\\\n"
"\\lambda_1 = 3\\\\\n"
"\\lambda_2 = 5 \\\\\n"
"\\lambda_3 = 7\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"\\right\\}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\left\\{\n"
"\\begin{array}{c}\n"
"\\lambda_0 = -7 \\\\\n"
"\\lambda_1 = 3\\\\\n"
"\\lambda_2 = 5 \\\\\n"
"\\lambda_3 = 7\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"\\right\\}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\left\\{\n"
"\\begin{array}{c}\n"
"|\\phi_0\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|00\\rangle + |11\\rangle)\\\\\n"
"|\\phi_1\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|00\\rangle - |11\\rangle)\\\\\n"
"|\\phi_2\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|01\\rangle + |10\\rangle)\\\\\n"
"|\\phi_3\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|01\\rangle - |10\\rangle)\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"\\right\\}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\left\\{\n"
"\\begin{array}{c}\n"
"|\\phi_0\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|00\\rangle + |11\\rangle)\\\\\n"
"|\\phi_1\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|00\\rangle - |11\\rangle)\\\\\n"
"|\\phi_2\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|01\\rangle + |10\\rangle)\\\\\n"
"|\\phi_3\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|01\\rangle - |10\\rangle)\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"\\right\\}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We'll be using the following function to calculate the overlap penalty. Note that this is still part of mapping the problem to quantum circuits. However, as discussed in the previous lesson, this function calculates the overlap between a current variational circuit and the optimized circuit from a previous, lower-energy/cost state obtained. The new circuit being generated also has to be transpiled to run on real hardware. We have seen this function before, used on a simulator. Here, we must already consider the transpiling and related optimization for when we use a real backend, hence the lines around `if realbackend == 1`. This is mixing a bit of step 2, but we will call out step 2 explicitly later.\n"
msgstr "Kita akan menggunakan fungsi berikut untuk menghitung penalti overlap. Perhatikan bahwa ini masih bagian dari pemetaan masalah ke Circuit kuantum. Namun, seperti yang dibahas di pelajaran sebelumnya, fungsi ini menghitung overlap antara Circuit variasional saat ini dan Circuit yang dioptimalkan dari state energi/biaya rendah sebelumnya yang diperoleh. Circuit baru yang dihasilkan juga harus di-transpile untuk dijalankan pada hardware nyata. Kita sudah melihat fungsi ini sebelumnya, digunakan pada simulator. Di sini, kita harus sudah mempertimbangkan transpiling dan optimisasi terkait untuk saat kita menggunakan backend nyata, oleh karena itu baris di sekitar `if realbackend == 1`. Ini sedikit mencampur langkah 2, tapi kita akan menyebutkan langkah 2 secara eksplisit nanti.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now we add VQD's cost function. Note that compared to the previous lesson, we now have two additional arguments (`realbackend` and `backend`) to help us with transpilation when we use real backends.\n"
msgstr "Sekarang kita tambahkan fungsi biaya VQD. Perhatikan bahwa dibandingkan pelajaran sebelumnya, kita sekarang memiliki dua argumen tambahan (`realbackend` dan `backend`) untuk membantu kita dengan transpilasi saat menggunakan backend nyata.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Once again, we will use simulators for debugging, and then move on to real hardware.\n"
msgstr "Sekali lagi, kita akan menggunakan simulator untuk debugging, lalu beralih ke hardware nyata.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here we introduce the number of states we wish to calculate, the penalties, and a set of initial parameters, x0.\n"
msgstr "Di sini kita memperkenalkan jumlah state yang ingin kita hitung, penalti, dan serangkaian parameter awal, x0.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We will now test the algorithm using simulators:\n"
msgstr "Kita sekarang akan menguji algoritma menggunakan simulator:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "These results are fairly close to the expected ones except for approximation error and global phase. We could adjust the tolerance on the classical optimizer and/or the penalties for statevector overlap to obtain more precise values.\n"
msgstr "Hasil ini cukup mendekati yang diharapkan kecuali untuk kesalahan aproksimasi dan fase global. Kita bisa menyesuaikan toleransi pada optimizer klasik dan/atau penalti untuk overlap statevector untuk mendapatkan nilai yang lebih presisi.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Change betas {#change-betas}"
msgstr "Ubah betas {#change-betas}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As mentioned in the previous lesson, the values of $\\vec{\\beta}$ should be bigger than the difference between eigenvalues. Let us see what happens when they do not satisfy that condition with $\\hat{O}_2$\n"
msgstr "Seperti yang disebutkan di pelajaran sebelumnya, nilai $\\vec{\\beta}$ harus lebih besar dari selisih antara nilai eigen. Mari kita lihat apa yang terjadi ketika kondisi itu tidak terpenuhi dengan $\\hat{O}_2$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{O}_2 = 2 II - 3 XX + 2 YY - 4 ZZ\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{O}_2 = 2 II - 3 XX + 2 YY - 4 ZZ\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "with eigenvalues\n"
msgstr "dengan nilai eigen\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This time, the optimizer returns the same state $|\\phi_0\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|00\\rangle + |11\\rangle)$ as a proposed solution to all eigenstates: which is clearly wrong. This happens because the betas were too small to penalize the minimum eigenstate in the successive cost functions. Therefore, it was not excluded from the effective search space in later iterations of the algorithm, and always chosen as the best possible solution.\n"
msgstr "Kali ini, optimizer mengembalikan state yang sama $|\\phi_0\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|00\\rangle + |11\\rangle)$ sebagai solusi yang diusulkan untuk semua eigenstate: yang jelas salah. Ini terjadi karena beta terlalu kecil untuk memberi penalti pada eigenstate minimum dalam fungsi biaya yang berurutan. Oleh karena itu, ia tidak dikecualikan dari ruang pencarian efektif pada iterasi algoritma berikutnya, dan selalu dipilih sebagai solusi terbaik yang mungkin.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We recommend experimenting with the values of $\\vec{\\beta}$, and ensuring they are bigger than the difference between eigenvalues.\n"
msgstr "Kami merekomendasikan untuk bereksperimen dengan nilai $\\vec{\\beta}$, dan memastikan nilainya lebih besar dari selisih antara nilai eigen.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum execution {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-execution}"
msgstr "Langkah 2: Optimalkan masalah untuk eksekusi kuantum {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-execution}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To run this on real hardware, we must optimize the quantum circuits for our quantum computer of choice. For our purposes here, we will simply use the least busy backend.\n"
msgstr "Untuk menjalankan ini pada hardware nyata, kita harus mengoptimalkan Circuit kuantum untuk komputer kuantum pilihan kita. Untuk tujuan di sini, kita cukup gunakan backend yang paling tidak sibuk.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We will transpile our circuit using a preset pass manager and optimization level 3.\n"
msgstr "Kita akan men-transpile Circuit menggunakan preset pass manager dan optimization level 3.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Execute using IBM Quantum primitives {#step-3-execute-using-ibm-quantum-primitives}"
msgstr "Langkah 3: Eksekusi menggunakan primitif IBM Quantum {#step-3-execute-using-ibm-quantum-primitives}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Taking care to reset our betas to sufficiently high values, we can now run our calculation on real quantum hardware.\n"
msgstr "Dengan memastikan beta kita diatur ke nilai yang cukup tinggi, kita sekarang bisa menjalankan perhitungan pada hardware kuantum nyata.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Post-process, return result in classical format {#step-4-post-process-return-result-in-classical-format}"
msgstr "Langkah 4: Post-process, kembalikan hasil dalam format klasik {#step-4-post-process-return-result-in-classical-format}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Our output is structurally similar to what has been discussed in previous lessons and examples. But there is something problematic in the results above, from which we can derive a cautionary message for the context of excited states. To limit computing time used on this learning example, we set a maximum number of iterations for classical optimizer that was potentially too low: 200 iterations. A previous calculation above, on a simulator, failed to converge in 200 iterations. Here, ours did converge... but to what tolerance? We have not specified a tolerance for COBYLA to consider itself \"converged\". A glance at the function value and comparison with previous runs tells us that COBYLA was not close to converging to the precision we require.\n"
msgstr "Output kita secara struktural mirip dengan yang telah dibahas di pelajaran dan contoh sebelumnya. Tapi ada sesuatu yang bermasalah dalam hasil di atas, dari mana kita bisa mendapatkan pesan peringatan untuk konteks excited state. Untuk membatasi waktu komputasi yang digunakan dalam contoh pembelajaran ini, kita menetapkan jumlah iterasi maksimum untuk optimizer klasik yang mungkin terlalu rendah: 200 iterasi. Perhitungan sebelumnya di atas, pada simulator, gagal konvergen dalam 200 iterasi. Di sini, kita berhasil konvergen... tapi dengan toleransi berapa? Kita tidak menentukan toleransi agar COBYLA menganggap dirinya \"konvergen\". Sekilas pada nilai fungsi dan perbandingan dengan run sebelumnya memberi tahu kita bahwa COBYLA tidak mendekati konvergensi ke presisi yang kita butuhkan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "There is another issue: the energy of the first excited state appears to be lower than the energy of the ground state! See if you can explain how this could happen. Hint: it is related to the convergence point we just addressed. This behavior is explained in detail below after VQD is applied to the H2 molecule.\n"
msgstr "Ada masalah lain: energi excited state pertama tampaknya lebih rendah dari energi ground state! Lihat apakah kamu bisa menjelaskan bagaimana ini bisa terjadi. Petunjuk: ini berkaitan dengan titik konvergensi yang baru saja kita bahas. Perilaku ini dijelaskan secara detail di bawah setelah VQD diterapkan pada molekul H2.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Quantum chemistry: ground state and excited energy solver {#quantum-chemistry-ground-state-and-excited-energy-solver}"
msgstr "Kimia kuantum: solver energi ground state dan excited state {#quantum-chemistry-ground-state-and-excited-energy-solver}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Our objective is to minimize the expectation value of the observable representing energy (Hamiltonian $\\hat{\\mathcal{H}}$):\n"
msgstr "Tujuan kita adalah meminimalkan nilai ekspektasi dari observable yang merepresentasikan energi (Hamiltonian $\\hat{\\mathcal{H}}$):\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\min_{\\vec\\theta} \\langle\\psi(\\vec\\theta)|\\hat{\\mathcal{H}}|\\psi(\\vec\\theta)\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\min_{\\vec\\theta} \\langle\\psi(\\vec\\theta)|\\hat{\\mathcal{H}}|\\psi(\\vec\\theta)\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/examples-and-applications/extracted-outputs/de006d72-db04-49d4-806b-89bd1e5b9947-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/examples-and-applications/extracted-outputs/de006d72-db04-49d4-806b-89bd1e5b9947-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can minimize this cost function to calculate optimal parameters, and we can check our code first by using a local simulator.\n"
msgstr "Kita bisa meminimalkan fungsi biaya ini untuk menghitung parameter optimal, dan kita bisa memeriksa kode kita terlebih dahulu menggunakan simulator lokal.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The minimum value of the cost function (-1.857...) is the ground state energy of the H2 molecule, in units of hartrees.\n"
msgstr "Nilai minimum dari fungsi biaya (-1.857...) adalah energi ground state dari molekul H2, dalam satuan hartree.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Excited States {#excited-states}"
msgstr "Excited States {#excited-states}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can also leverage VQD to solve for $k=2$ total states (the ground state and the first excited state).\n"
msgstr "Kita juga bisa memanfaatkan VQD untuk memecahkan $k=2$ total state (ground state dan excited state pertama).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We'll add our overlap calculation:\n"
msgstr "Kita akan tambahkan perhitungan overlap kita:\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Real hardware and a final cautionary message {#real-hardware-and-a-final-cautionary-message}"
msgstr "Hardware nyata dan pesan peringatan terakhir {#real-hardware-and-a-final-cautionary-message}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We will use a preset pass manager for transpilation, and we will maximally optimize our circuit using optimization level 3.\n"
msgstr "Kita akan menggunakan preset pass manager untuk transpilasi, dan kita akan memaksimalkan optimisasi Circuit menggunakan optimization level 3.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because VQD is highly iterative, we will carry out all steps inside a Runtime session, such that our jobs will only be queued at the beginning, and not between every parameter update. Nothing else changes about the syntax for the cost function or estimator.\n"
msgstr "Karena VQD sangat iteratif, kita akan menjalankan semua langkah di dalam Runtime Session, sehingga job kita hanya akan di-queue di awal, dan bukan di antara setiap pembaruan parameter. Tidak ada yang berubah dari sintaks untuk fungsi biaya atau Estimator.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The ground state energy obtained (-1.83 hartrees) is not too far from the correct value (-1.85 hartrees). However, the excited state energy is quite a bit off. This is similar to the erroneous behavior we saw earlier in this lesson. The energy reported for the excited state is nearly the same as that for the ground state. In the previous case, we even saw an excited state energy that was _lower_ than the reported ground state energy.\n"
msgstr "Energi ground state yang diperoleh (-1.83 hartree) tidak terlalu jauh dari nilai yang benar (-1.85 hartree). Namun, energi excited state cukup meleset. Ini mirip dengan perilaku keliru yang kita lihat sebelumnya dalam pelajaran ini. Energi yang dilaporkan untuk excited state hampir sama dengan energi ground state. Dalam kasus sebelumnya, kita bahkan melihat energi excited state yang _lebih rendah_ dari energi ground state yang dilaporkan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "It is not possible for a variational calculation to yield an energy that is lower than the true ground state energy. In the earlier instance, the ground state energy we obtained was not very close to the true ground state. Since we did not obtain the true ground state energy in that case, there is no contradiction. In the present case, the ground state energy was fairly close to the correct value, and yet the excited state energy seems strangely close to that same value.\n"
msgstr "Tidak mungkin kalkulasi variasional menghasilkan energi yang lebih rendah dari energi ground state yang sebenarnya. Dalam kasus sebelumnya, energi ground state yang kita peroleh tidak terlalu dekat dengan ground state yang sebenarnya. Karena kita tidak memperoleh energi ground state yang sebenarnya dalam kasus itu, tidak ada kontradiksi. Dalam kasus ini, energi ground state cukup dekat dengan nilai yang benar, namun energi excited state tampaknya anehnya dekat dengan nilai yang sama.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To understand better how this happened, recall that the way we find an excited state is by requiring that the variational state be orthogonal to the ground state (using the overlap circuits and penalty terms). If we fail to obtain an accurate ground state energy (or are off by a few percent), then we also fail to obtain an accurate ground state vector! So when we require that the excited state be orthogonal to the first state we found, we were not imposing orthogonality with the true ground state, but rather with some approximation of it (sometimes a poor approximation of it). Thus, the excited state was not forced to be orthogonal to the true ground state, and our energy estimates for the excited states were actually quite close to the ground state energy.\n"
msgstr "Untuk lebih memahami bagaimana ini terjadi, ingat bahwa cara kita menemukan excited state adalah dengan mensyaratkan bahwa state variasional ortogonal terhadap ground state (menggunakan overlap Circuit dan suku penalti). Jika kita gagal mendapatkan energi ground state yang akurat (atau meleset beberapa persen), maka kita juga gagal mendapatkan vektor ground state yang akurat! Jadi ketika kita mensyaratkan bahwa excited state ortogonal terhadap state pertama yang kita temukan, kita tidak memberlakukan ortogonalitas dengan ground state yang sebenarnya, melainkan dengan suatu aproksimasi dari ground state tersebut (terkadang aproksimasi yang buruk). Dengan demikian, excited state tidak dipaksa untuk ortogonal terhadap ground state yang sebenarnya, dan estimasi energi kita untuk excited state sebenarnya cukup dekat dengan energi ground state.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This will always be a concern in VQD. But in principle, this can be corrected by increasing the maximum number of iterations for the classical optimizer, imposing lower tolerance for the classical optimizer, and possibly also trying a different ansatz if we are habitually missing the true ground state. As we have seen, one may also need to modify the overlap penalties (betas). But that is really a separate issue. No penalty for overlap will keep you away from the true ground state, if you haven't found a very good estimate of the true ground state for the overlap circuit.\n"
msgstr "Ini akan selalu menjadi perhatian dalam VQD. Tapi pada prinsipnya, ini bisa dikoreksi dengan meningkatkan jumlah iterasi maksimum untuk optimizer klasik, memberlakukan toleransi lebih rendah untuk optimizer klasik, dan mungkin juga mencoba ansatz yang berbeda jika kita secara konsisten gagal menemukan ground state yang sebenarnya. Seperti yang kita lihat, seseorang mungkin juga perlu memodifikasi penalti overlap (beta). Tapi itu sebenarnya masalah yang terpisah. Tidak ada penalti untuk overlap yang akan membuat kamu menjauh dari ground state yang sebenarnya, jika kamu belum menemukan estimasi yang sangat baik dari ground state yang sebenarnya untuk overlap Circuit.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Optimization: max-cut {#optimization-max-cut}"
msgstr "Optimasi: Max-Cut {#optimization-max-cut}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The maximum cut (max-cut) problem is a combinatorial optimization problem that involves dividing the vertices of a graph into two disjoint sets such that the number of edges between the two sets is maximized. More formally, given an undirected graph $G=(V,E)$, where $V$ is the set of vertices and $E$ is the set of edges, the max-cut problem asks to partition the vertices into two disjoint subsets, $S$ and $T$, such that the number of edges with one endpoint in $S$ and the other in $T$ is maximized.\n"
msgstr "Masalah potongan maksimum (Max-Cut) adalah masalah optimasi kombinatorial yang melibatkan pembagian simpul-simpul sebuah graf menjadi dua himpunan terpisah sehingga jumlah sisi antara kedua himpunan tersebut dimaksimalkan. Lebih formal, diberikan graf tak berarah $G=(V,E)$, di mana $V$ adalah himpunan simpul dan $E$ adalah himpunan sisi, masalah Max-Cut meminta kita untuk mempartisi simpul-simpul menjadi dua himpunan terpisah, $S$ dan $T$, sehingga jumlah sisi dengan satu titik ujung di $S$ dan titik ujung lainnya di $T$ dimaksimalkan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can apply max-cut to solve a various problems, such as clustering, network design, and phase transitions. We'll start by creating a problem graph:\n"
msgstr "Kita bisa menerapkan Max-Cut untuk menyelesaikan berbagai masalah, seperti pengelompokan, desain jaringan, dan transisi fase. Kita mulai dengan membuat graf masalah:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/examples-and-applications/extracted-outputs/3eb71b79-a988-4807-aa88-7fb25a78a236-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/examples-and-applications/extracted-outputs/3eb71b79-a988-4807-aa88-7fb25a78a236-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This problem can be expressed as a binary optimization problem. For each node $0 \\leq i < n$, where $n$ is the number of nodes of the graph (in this case $n=4$), we will consider the binary variable $x_i$. This variable will have the value $1$ if node $i$ is one of the groups that we'll label $1$ and $0$ if it's in the other group, that we'll label as $0$. We will also denote as $w_{ij}$ (element $(i,j)$ of the adjacency matrix $w$) the weight of the edge that goes from node $i$ to node $j$. Because the graph is undirected, $w_{ij}=w_{ji}$. Then we can formulate our problem as maximizing the following cost function:\n"
msgstr "Masalah ini bisa diekspresikan sebagai masalah optimasi biner. Untuk setiap simpul $0 \\leq i < n$, di mana $n$ adalah jumlah simpul pada graf (dalam hal ini $n=4$), kita akan mempertimbangkan variabel biner $x_i$. Variabel ini akan bernilai $1$ jika simpul $i$ berada di salah satu grup yang kita beri label $1$ dan $0$ jika berada di grup lainnya, yang kita beri label $0$. Kita juga akan menyebut $w_{ij}$ (elemen $(i,j)$ dari matriks ketetanggaan $w$) sebagai bobot sisi yang menghubungkan simpul $i$ ke simpul $j$. Karena graf tak berarah, $w_{ij}=w_{ji}$. Maka kita bisa merumuskan masalah kita sebagai memaksimalkan fungsi biaya berikut:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"C(\\vec{x})\n"
"& =\\sum_{i,j=0}^n w_{ij} x_i(1-x_j)\\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"C(\\vec{x})\n"
"& =\\sum_{i,j=0}^n w_{ij} x_i(1-x_j)\\\\[1mm]\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "& = \\sum_{i,j=0}^n w_{ij} x_i - \\sum_{i,j=0}^n w_{ij} x_ix_j\\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr "& = \\sum_{i,j=0}^n w_{ij} x_i - \\sum_{i,j=0}^n w_{ij} x_ix_j\\\\[1mm]\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"& = \\sum_{i,j=0}^n w_{ij} x_i - \\sum_{i=0}^n \\sum_{j=0}^i 2w_{ij} x_ix_j\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"& = \\sum_{i,j=0}^n w_{ij} x_i - \\sum_{i=0}^n \\sum_{j=0}^i 2w_{ij} x_ix_j\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To solve this problem with a quantum computer, we are going to express the cost function as the expected value of an observable. However, the observables that Qiskit admits natively consist of Pauli operators, that have eigenvalues $1$ and $-1$ instead of $0$ and $1$. That's why we are going to make the following change of variable:\n"
msgstr "Untuk menyelesaikan masalah ini dengan komputer kuantum, kita akan mengekspresikan fungsi biaya sebagai nilai ekspektasi dari sebuah observable. Namun, observable yang Qiskit dukung secara native terdiri dari operator Pauli, yang memiliki nilai eigen $1$ dan $-1$ bukan $0$ dan $1$. Itulah mengapa kita akan melakukan perubahan variabel berikut:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Where $\\vec{x}=(x_0,x_1,\\cdots ,x_{n-1})$. We can use the adjacency matrix $w$ to comfortably access the weights of all the edge. This will be used to obtain our cost function:\n"
msgstr "Di mana $\\vec{x}=(x_0,x_1,\\cdots ,x_{n-1})$. Kita bisa menggunakan matriks ketetanggaan $w$ untuk mengakses bobot semua sisi dengan mudah. Ini akan digunakan untuk mendapatkan fungsi biaya kita:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"z_i = 1-2x_i \\rightarrow x_i = \\frac{1-z_i}{2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"z_i = 1-2x_i \\rightarrow x_i = \\frac{1-z_i}{2}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This implies that:\n"
msgstr "Ini berarti bahwa:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{lcl} x_i=0 & \\rightarrow & z_i=1 \\\\ x_i=1 & \\rightarrow & z_i=-1.\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{lcl} x_i=0 & \\rightarrow & z_i=1 \\\\ x_i=1 & \\rightarrow & z_i=-1.\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "So the new cost function we want to maximize is:\n"
msgstr "Sehingga fungsi biaya baru yang ingin kita maksimalkan adalah:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"C(\\vec{z})\n"
"& = \\sum_{i,j=0}^n w_{ij} \\bigg(\\frac{1-z_i}{2}\\bigg)\\bigg(1-\\frac{1-z_j}{2}\\bigg)\\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"C(\\vec{z})\n"
"& = \\sum_{i,j=0}^n w_{ij} \\bigg(\\frac{1-z_i}{2}\\bigg)\\bigg(1-\\frac{1-z_j}{2}\\bigg)\\\\[1mm]\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "& = \\sum_{i,j=0}^n \\frac{w_{ij}}{4} - \\sum_{i,j=0}^n \\frac{w_{ij}}{4} z_iz_j\\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr "& = \\sum_{i,j=0}^n \\frac{w_{ij}}{4} - \\sum_{i,j=0}^n \\frac{w_{ij}}{4} z_iz_j\\\\[1mm]\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"& = \\sum_{i=0}^n \\sum_{j=0}^i \\frac{w_{ij}}{2} -  \\sum_{i=0}^n \\sum_{j=0}^i \\frac{w_{ij}}{2} z_iz_j\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"& = \\sum_{i=0}^n \\sum_{j=0}^i \\frac{w_{ij}}{2} -  \\sum_{i=0}^n \\sum_{j=0}^i \\frac{w_{ij}}{2} z_iz_j\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Moreover, the natural tendency of a quantum computer is to find minima (usually the lowest energy) instead of maxima so instead of maximizing $C(\\vec{z})$ we are going to minimize:\n"
msgstr "Selain itu, kecenderungan alami komputer kuantum adalah mencari minima (biasanya energi terendah) bukan maksima, sehingga alih-alih memaksimalkan $C(\\vec{z})$ kita akan meminimalkan:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"-C(\\vec{z}) =  \\sum_{i=0}^n \\sum_{j=0}^i \\frac{w_{ij}}{2} z_iz_j -  \\sum_{i=0}^n \\sum_{j=0}^i \\frac{w_{ij}}{2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"-C(\\vec{z}) =  \\sum_{i=0}^n \\sum_{j=0}^i \\frac{w_{ij}}{2} z_iz_j -  \\sum_{i=0}^n \\sum_{j=0}^i \\frac{w_{ij}}{2}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now that we have a cost function to minimize whose variables can have the values $-1$ and $1$, we can make the following analogy with the Pauli $Z$:\n"
msgstr "Sekarang kita sudah punya fungsi biaya yang akan diminimalkan dengan variabel yang bisa bernilai $-1$ dan $1$, kita bisa membuat analogi berikut dengan Pauli $Z$:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"z_i \\equiv Z_i = \\overbrace{I}^{n-1}\\otimes ... \\otimes \\overbrace{Z}^{i} \\otimes ... \\otimes \\overbrace{I}^{0}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"z_i \\equiv Z_i = \\overbrace{I}^{n-1}\\otimes ... \\otimes \\overbrace{Z}^{i} \\otimes ... \\otimes \\overbrace{I}^{0}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In other words, the variable $z_i$ will be equivalent to a $Z$ gate acting on qubit $i$. Moreover:\n"
msgstr "Dengan kata lain, variabel $z_i$ akan setara dengan Gate $Z$ yang bekerja pada qubit $i$. Selain itu:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"Z_i|x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0\\rangle = z_i|x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0\\rangle \\rightarrow \\langle x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0 |Z_i|x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0\\rangle = z_i\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"Z_i|x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0\\rangle = z_i|x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0\\rangle \\rightarrow \\langle x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0 |Z_i|x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0\\rangle = z_i\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Then the observable we are going to consider is:\n"
msgstr "Maka observable yang akan kita pertimbangkan adalah:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{H} = \\sum_{i=0}^n \\sum_{j=0}^i \\frac{w_{ij}}{2} Z_iZ_j\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{H} = \\sum_{i=0}^n \\sum_{j=0}^i \\frac{w_{ij}}{2} Z_iZ_j\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "to which we will have to add the independent term afterwards:\n"
msgstr "yang kemudian harus kita tambahkan suku independen setelahnya:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\texttt{offset} = - \\sum_{i=0}^n \\sum_{j=0}^i \\frac{w_{ij}}{2}\n"
"$$\n"
"The operator is a linear combination of terms with Z operators on nodes connected by an edge (recall that the 0th qubit is farthest right): $IIZZ + IZIZ + IZZI + ZIIZ + ZZII$. Once the operator is constructed, the ansatz for the QAOA algorithm can easily be built by using the `QAOAAnsatz` circuit from the Qiskit circuit library.\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\texttt{offset} = - \\sum_{i=0}^n \\sum_{j=0}^i \\frac{w_{ij}}{2}\n"
"$$\n"
"Operator ini adalah kombinasi linier dari suku-suku dengan operator Z pada simpul yang terhubung oleh sisi (ingat bahwa qubit ke-0 ada di paling kanan): $IIZZ + IZIZ + IZZI + ZIIZ + ZZII$. Setelah operator dibuat, ansatz untuk algoritma QAOA bisa dengan mudah dibangun menggunakan Circuit `QAOAAnsatz` dari pustaka Circuit Qiskit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/examples-and-applications/extracted-outputs/d28c4262-a080-4fe4-9427-762326184cd8-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/examples-and-applications/extracted-outputs/d28c4262-a080-4fe4-9427-762326184cd8-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We now set an initial set of random parameters:\n"
msgstr "Sekarang kita atur set parameter acak awal:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Any classical optimizer can be used to minimize the cost function. On a real quantum system, an optimizer designed for non-smooth cost function landscapes usually does better. Here we use the [COBYLA routine](https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/optimize.minimize-cobyla.html#optimize-minimize-cobyla) from SciPy via the minimize function.\n"
msgstr "Optimizer klasik apa pun bisa digunakan untuk meminimalkan fungsi biaya. Pada sistem kuantum nyata, optimizer yang dirancang untuk lanskap fungsi biaya yang tidak mulus biasanya menghasilkan hasil lebih baik. Di sini kita menggunakan [rutinitas COBYLA](https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/optimize.minimize-cobyla.html#optimize-minimize-cobyla) dari SciPy melalui fungsi minimize.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Because we are iteratively executing many calls to Runtime, we make use of a session to execute all calls within a single block. Moreover, for QAOA, the solution is encoded in the output distribution of the ansatz circuit bound with the optimal parameters from the minimization. Therefore, we will need a Sampler primitive, and will instantiate it with the same session\n"
"And run our minimization routine:\n"
msgstr "Karena kita menjalankan banyak panggilan ke Runtime secara iteratif, kita menggunakan sebuah Session untuk menjalankan semua panggilan dalam satu blok. Selain itu, untuk QAOA, solusinya tersandi dalam distribusi output dari Circuit ansatz yang diikat dengan parameter optimal dari minimasi. Oleh karena itu, kita akan memerlukan primitif Sampler, dan akan menginisialisasinya dengan Session yang sama. Lalu jalankan rutinitas minimasi kita:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The solution vector of parameter angles (`x`), when plugged into the ansatz circuit, yields the graph partitioning that we were looking for.\n"
msgstr "Vektor solusi sudut parameter (`x`), ketika dimasukkan ke dalam Circuit ansatz, menghasilkan partisi graf yang kita cari.\n"

